    "ui.about_bildhaft": "bildhaft",
    "ui.about_bildhaft_url": "https://lautstark.github.io/bildhaft/",
    "ui.about_lead": "vorlaut is the editor for a small talker: five keys that are displays at the same time. The sets, the symbols and the sentences are made here, and out of them come the pictures and sound files that go onto the device.",
    "ui.about_leaves": "Your sets, your sentences and your METACOM files stay here - there is no server and there are no accounts. What does go out: single search words to ARASAAC, the one-off download of an offline voice, the library that lets that voice compute, and - only with a key of your own - the sentence itself to Azure. The privacy notice says where each of those goes.",
    "ui.about_leaves_head": "What leaves this computer",
    "ui.about_mitreden": "mitreden",
    "ui.about_mitreden_url": "https://lautstark.github.io/mitreden/",
    "ui.about_repo": "github.com/Lautstark/vorlaut",
    "ui.about_repo_url": "https://github.com/Lautstark/vorlaut",
    "ui.about_source": "vorlaut is open source under the MIT licence. mitreden turns a sentence into an audio file, so that every device speaks with the same voice; bildhaft turns typed sentences into rows of symbols to print.",
    "ui.about_source_head": "Source code and sister projects",
    "ui.about_symbols": "The pictograms come from ARASAAC and are licensed CC BY-NC-SA - nothing taken from them may be used commercially. METACOM needs a licence: vorlaut ships no METACOM symbols, it reads your own licensed folder. The offline voices are Piper models and compute in the browser.",
